{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/bioetl/application/pipelines/common/transformer_initialization.py","codegenInstructions":"","suggestions":["def build_runtime_transformer_init(\n    default_provider: str,\n    default_entity_type: str,\n    *,\n    owner_type: type[object],\n) -> Callable[..., None]:\n    \"\"\"Return a shared runtime-generated ``__init__`` for transformer subclasses.\n\n    ``owner_type`` must be the class that installs the generated initializer so\n    subclass inheritance does not recurse through the same generated method.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _runtime_init(\n        self: Any,  # Any: runtime method to bypass architecture checks\n        provider: str = default_provider,\n        entity_type: str = default_entity_type,\n        silver_filters: SilverFilterConfig | None = None,\n        gold_filters: GoldFilterConfig | None = None,\n        tracer: TracingPort | None = None,\n        metrics: MetricsPort | None = None,\n        identity_service: EntityIdentityGenerator | None = None,\n        pii_hasher: PiiHasherPort | None = None,\n        dependencies: TransformerDependencyContext | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        initialize_next_transformer_mro(\n            self,\n            owner_type,\n            provider=provider,\n            kwargs=transformer_init_kwargs(locals()),\n        )\n\n    _runtime_init.__name__ = \"__init__\"\n    _runtime_init.__qualname__ = \"__init__\"\n    _runtime_init.__doc__ = \"Shared runtime-generated transformer constructor.\"\n    return _runtime_init"],"comment":"**Optional `owner_type` creates an infinite-recursion trap.**\n\nWhen `owner_type` is `None`, line 85 sets `mro_owner = type(self)`. `initialize_next_transformer_mro` then calls `super(type(self), self).__init__(...)`. If a subclass inherits this generated `__init__` without installing its own, `type(self)` is the subclass, `super()` resolves back to the class that holds the same generated function, and the call recurses until `RecursionError`. This is the classic `super(type(self), self)` bug.\n\nThe docstring already states `owner_type` \"must be the class that installs the generated initializer\". Make that a requirement in the signature instead of a comment.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def build_runtime_transformer_init(\n     default_provider: str,\n     default_entity_type: str,\n     *,\n-    owner_type: type[object] | None = None,\n+    owner_type: type[object],\n ) -> Callable[..., None]:\n@@\n-        mro_owner = owner_type if owner_type is not None else type(self)\n         initialize_next_transformer_mro(\n             self,\n-            mro_owner,\n+            owner_type,\n             provider=provider,\n             kwargs=transformer_init_kwargs(locals()),\n         )\n```\n\n`build_runtime_publication_transformer_init` in `publication_transformer_context.py` (lines 130, 140) must then require `owner_type` as well.\n</details>"}
